# composer.lock and package-lock.json are deliberately TRACKED, and matter more
# now that vendor/vendor-prefixed/ is built rather than committed: the locks are the
# only thing pinning which versions Strauss prefixes. .distignore keeps them out
# of the zip.
#
# vendor/vendor-prefixed/ is Strauss output. `composer strauss` rebuilds it, and
# bin/package.mjs refuses to build a zip without it, because a zip missing it
# installs cleanly and then fatals on the first query.
#
# The lock files carried by the vendored libraries themselves are a different
# thing and stay out: they record those libraries' own dev dependencies, which
# mean nothing once Strauss has flattened the code into our namespace.
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/

# Local wp-env override (machine-specific plugin paths)
.wp-env.override.json
/.wp-env/

# Internal working material. This plugin is going to be open sourced, so
# anything that is not shipped code stays out of the repo: planning docs,
# competitor research, and above all the QA findings, which describe how to
# attack the product. Their home is ~/Local Sites/dono/dono-pro-addon-specs/.
/docs/
/qa/
# Working notes for whoever is building this, not for whoever is reading it:
# it describes the Pro add-on line and the licensing model, which have no place
# in the free core's public repo. Kept on disk, just not published.
CLAUDE.md
# Internal engineering direction: what we deferred, declined and are watching.
# Useful to us, useful to a competitor, and not shipped code.
ROADMAP.md

# Packaged zips from `npm run package`.
/dist/

# make-pot scratch: the intermediate @dono/ui template, see "npm run i18n".
/.cache

# graphify knowledge graph: an 8MB graph.json rebuilt from source on demand.
# The nested one is where the AST extractor writes its cache when handed a
# subdirectory, so ignore it at any depth rather than only at the root.
graphify-out/
